    },
    "body": "S improves development loss, but its saved conditional older-prefix intervention does not demonstrate useful history. This review preserves the verified Q/S/L numerical result and corrects history/optimization attribution, zero CPX3 tokenizer binding, incomplete CPQK continuation, missing executable provenance, and cost/cycle claims.\n\nSpecify one next DeepSeek task: repair metadata and redundant inference work, then replay frozen S through identity corners, direct row ablations and a fit-only length-conditioned mean-history comparator. Replicate on deterministically selected unused positions in the existing dev documents. No fitting or new architecture is executed in this review; selective maintenance and exact memory remain later roadmap responsibilities.\n\nSynchronize README, canonical dependencies, current state, direction, project map, continuation and evidence/resource interpretation. Keep historical receipts and artifacts intact. The proposed allowance is not applied; the live ledger remains 176138565/178100000 ms.\n\nValidation: saved artifact sets/hashes, development vectors/intervals and donor map independently reconstructed; source audit of gradients/dose/artifact/resume; independent mathematical review of the handoff; claim-wording gate, relative links in all 12 documents and git diff --check pass. No Rust build, training or model forward ran. Queue acknowledgements are not model tests.\n\nReferences #973, #820, #963, #964. Broad acceptance remains open.\n",
